 ## Background
-The concept of piecewise linear transfer functions has been widely adopted in volume rendering to provide intuitive control over visualization parameters. The integration of these functions, particularly using hardware-accelerated texture lookups for exponential opacity calculations, was highlighted in surveys of GPU-based volume rendering of unstructured grids [S2, unofficial]. The use of power functions for opacity mapping to enhance gradient-based features was introduced in early volume illustration work [S1].
+The concept of piecewise linear transfer functions has been widely adopted in volume rendering to provide intuitive control over visualization parameters [G]. The integration of piecewise linear transfer functions using a 2D texture map, parameterized by opacity and thickness to compute the correct exponential per-pixel opacity, was described in a rendering system for GPU-based volume rendering of unstructured grids [S2, unofficial]. The use of power functions for opacity mapping to enhance gradient-based features was introduced in early volume illustration work [S1].
 
